{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima feels like a natural next choice after 10.000 Days because I want to explore more of Tool's intricate, progressive heaviness.",
    "The Sickness connects directly to my recent interest in Ten Thousand Fists, while City of Evil offers the energetic riffs and melodic guitar work I want right now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger fits the heavy side of my listening, but its raw, abrasive sound misses the melody and intricate playing I am seeking today.",
    "World Coming Down's slower, darker atmosphere is less appealing right now than music with energy or complexity."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The suggestions seem to treat heaviness as enough of a connection, although groove, melody, pace and intricate playing affect my choices differently.",
    "Broad overlap with my rock and metal listening explains several suggestions, but that alone does not make every familiar-sounding album a priority today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest listens to Tool and Disturbed make exploring more from those artists especially appealing now.",
    "I can enjoy melodic heavy albums such as Fallen, Hybrid Theory and Meteora without wanting to choose them this visit; my strongest interest today is in direct artist connections or energetic, intricate guitar work."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in heavy music, but only some captured the artist connections, melody and intricate energy driving my choices today."
}"}
